  "vibe_title_en": "Organic Melancholy",
  "master_prompt": "A hyper-realistic, macro portrait of The Protagonist situated in a sun-drenched, humid botanical preservation lab. The subject&#x27;s face is artistically adhered with translucent, vibrant yellow flower petals placed beneath the eyes to mimic organic, flowing tears. The skin texture is emphasized with a wet, glossy sheen, highlighting individual pores, vellus hairs, and the physical thickness of the petals. Lighting is a dramatic, high-contrast &#x27;hard sun&#x27; look, where a single shaft of light strikes the eyes and petals, casting the rest of the face into deep, soft shadow (chiaroscuro). Shot on a Hasselblad H6D-100c with a 120mm Macro lens at f/2.8 to create an extremely shallow depth of field that blurs the background into abstract grey-green tones. The aesthetic is strictly analog, simulating Kodak Portra 160 film with fine grain, warm skin tones, and zero digital plasticity. No neon.",
